<title>UK: British Airways resolves Paris airport row.</title>
<headline>British Airways resolves Paris airport row.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Tuesday it had resolved its disagreement over security surrounding Air Algerie's check-in facilities at Charles de Gaulle airport in Paris, allowing the UK carrier to resume full services, after a seven-week dispute.</p>
<p>BA had been closing its check-in counters at the airport for several hours each day after Air Algerie, the state airline of war-torn Algeria, was allowed to resume flights from Paris after a two year break. BA has arranged with Charles de Gaulle airport authorities to have separate check-in facilities at a temporary location at Terminal 1.</p>
</text>
